    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230-a1">

                <pb facs="0286" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg252"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 114.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >State Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Answering your and Reid’s telegrams, Secretary Navy authorizes admiral remain
                    with <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> at Portsmouth during admiralty
                    festivities and advises him, owing illness of daughter, need not return on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> to United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
